{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>You shall not slaughter upon leavened bread the blood of My sacrifice.</b> Ramban, of blessed memory, explained: it should have said לא תזבח על חמץ זבחי, for the blood is not slaughtered; and it comes to teach the saying of the Rabbis, of blessed memory: 'one may not slaughter the Paschal offering while leavened bread still exists.' But the measure of the verse is: לא תזבח על חמץ — 'you shall not slaughter upon leavened bread' — and likewise ולא דם זבחי יהיה על חמץ — 'and the blood of My sacrifice shall not be upon leavened bread' — and it comes to teach two things: that one may not slaughter the Paschal offering while leavened bread still exists, and that one may not sprinkle the blood while leavened bread still exists."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:20.047411680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}